{
  "title": "Migrate remaining historical game exports to v9 snake_case",
  "description": "The export pipeline now supports game export v9 with snake_case wire keys, and the season 2 committed exports were migrated as part of the initial schema rollout. The remaining historical exports in `website/public/games/` are still stored on disk as v8 camelCase JSON.\n\
\n\
Finish the data migration in a follow-up, data-focused PR:\n\
- rewrite the remaining committed season 0 and season 1 exports to version 9\n\
- keep the file contents semantically identical apart from the version bump and key renames\n\
- regenerate any derived website data that depends on the committed exports if the migration changes it\n\
- run `make check` after the migration so schema validation, website loaders, and leaderboard generation all exercise the migrated files\n\
\n\
This should stay separate from the schema/code PR so review stays manageable and GitHub does not have to render the full code change plus hundreds of migrated export files at once.",
